---
import Layout from '../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
const example = `{
  "id": "agdr-12",
  "related": [
    { "rel": "implements", "type": "orbit.execution-slice", "id": "slice-004" },
    { "rel": "satisfies", "type": "orbit.acceptance-criterion", "id": "ac-2" }
  ],
  "extensions": {}
}`;
---
<Layout title="Interoperability"><section class="page"><p class="eyebrow">Interoperability profile · v0.1</p><h1>Small artefacts can compose.</h1><p class="lede">Agent SDLC standards use stable identifiers, typed relationships, optional URIs, version conventions, producer metadata, and namespaced extensions.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Informative profile.</strong> ORBIT and AgDR remain independently conformant. These relationships are optional until adopted normatively.</div><pre class="code">{example}</pre><h2>Relationship shape</h2><p>A relationship has a <code>rel</code>, a registered or URI-like <code>type</code>, and a target <code>id</code>. An optional <code>href</code> gives a portable URI. Targets MAY be unresolved. Relationship order has no meaning and duplicate relationship objects SHOULD be avoided.</p><h2>Initial relationship vocabulary</h2><p>related-to · implements · contributes-to · satisfies · derived-from · supersedes · decision-record · deliberation-record</p></section></Layout>
